# Pairs with SagaCompletes. Reproduces production before #4474 was fixed
# (#4516): a saga bound
# to the resized copy R, whose resize is undone after the swap, sends its
# terminals to R directly. The routed-logical stamp is stripped, so R's undo
# redirect does not refuse them, and R takes them until the undo discards it;
# from then on R's shards are deleted and AppendTxTerminalAsync throws
# InvalidOperationException, which the broadcast does not follow. The saga never
# completes. A second edit lets the stalled saga count as quiescent, so the
# mutant cannot deadlock and the liveness property is the only thing TLC can
# report. The naive fix, following that refusal to the old copy, is
# AtomicOnOwnerDiscardedCopyTerminalRedirects.
MODULE: SagaCompletesDiscardedCopyRefusesTerminal
TARGET: SagaCompletes
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: a saga bound to a copy an undo discarded can never deliver its remaining terminals
PERTURBS: SagaTerminal

--- FIND
    /\ s \in TermTargets \ told
    /\ told' = told \cup {s}
--- REPLACE
    /\ s \in TermTargets \ told
\* MUTATION: the discarded copy refuses the terminal outright.
    /\ ~(bound = R /\ ~Live(R))
    /\ told' = told \cup {s}
--- END

--- FIND
Quiescent ==
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"}
--- REPLACE
Quiescent ==
\* MUTATION: a saga stalled on a discarded copy is not in flight.
    /\ sg \in {"idle", "done"} \/ (bound = R /\ ~Live(R))
--- END